    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/cyberseconto/R8aF2oKT2FTlP9n9dgKY847">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/cyberseconto/R8XQlC41lT0F81B33a15WBU"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en-us">Certified Information Systems Security Professional (CISSP) is an independent information security certification granted by the International Information System Security Certification Consortium, also known as (ISC)².

As of January 1, 2020 there are 142,112 (ISC)² members holding the CISSP certification worldwide, in 170 countries with the United States holding the highest member count at 90,514 members (63.4%). In June 2004, the CISSP designation was accredited under the ANSI ISO/IEC Standard 17024:2003. It is also formally approved by the U.S. Department of Defense (DoD) in their Information Assurance Technical (IAT), Managerial (IAM), and System Architect and Engineer (IASAE) categories for their DoDD 8570 certification requirement.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CISSP</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://www.isc2.org/Certifications/CISSP"/>
    </owl:Class>
    


