        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/cyberseconto/R9277EQmmS28jh9TQF9PhP3"/>
        <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PEC0006	Acting fairly</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://w3id.org/cyberseconto/RDEzQSoAQnDqkzV86Y9IpgG -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/cyberseconto/RDEzQSoAQnDqkzV86Y9IpgG">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/cyberseconto/Tactics"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The adversary is trying to run malicious code.

Execution consists of techniques that result in adversary-controlled code running on a local or remote system. Techniques that run malicious code are often paired with techniques from all other tactics to achieve broader goals, like exploring a network or stealing data. For example, an adversary might use a remote access tool to run a PowerShell script that does Remote System Discovery.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Execution</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">TA0002</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


