    <!-- https://w3id.org/cyberseconto/RDL6x98zreFGeL72CR5x3GP -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/cyberseconto/RDL6x98zreFGeL72CR5x3GP">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/cyberseconto/RxmJxtXZVpBevfBGgiNv2X"/>
        <rdfs:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">This course brings to students fundamental concepts in data and database security, and exposes them to latest research advances and practical techniques in protecting today’s database management systems and applications.
Access control in relational databases; grant/revoke model; cascading and non-cascading revoke; timestamp-based revoke; security by views; query modification; Oracle VPD; Truman and non-Truman models; auditing in databases; information warfare in databases; multi-level database security; polyinstantiation and covert channel; statistical database security; inference control; security by auditing; microaggregation; microdata security; random perturbation; watermarking and fingerprinting databases; XML database security; encrypted databases; SQL injection attack; schema randomization; anomaly detection in databases; P3P; privacy legislation; Hippocratic databases; perfect secrecy-based privacy;
k-anonymity model; l-diversity; indistinguishibility; privacy-preserving data mining; multi-party privacy preserving computation; privacy in OLAP.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Database Security and Privacy (Information Systems Engineering, INSE 6160)</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


